        <body>
            <div xml:id="d472">

                <pb facs="1211" n="1173" xml:id="pg1173"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">
                    Eisenhower Library, Hagerty papers</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Excerpt From the Diary of James C. Hagerty, Press Secretary to the President
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-06-18">June 18, 1954</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>In at 8:15.</p>
                <p>
                    Allen Dulles called early in the morning
                    to tell me that his organization expected there would be an anti-Communist
                    uprising in Guatemala very shortly. Officially we don’t know anything about it.
                    The story broke late Friday night.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
